course: dictionary
lesson: 8401
title: Ruin: spoil it or fall to bits
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To ruin something means to spoil it so badly that it is no good any more. «Rain ruined the picnic» means the rain spoilt it, so nobody could enjoy it. Ruin is a verb, so you may also see ruins, ruined and ruining.
explain: Ruin can also be a noun, meaning what is left of an old building that has fallen down. In history lessons you may visit the ruins of a castle. Look at the clues: old, fallen and stones tell you it means the broken remains of a building.
explain: Try the swap test. «One speck of dust can ruin a chip» still makes sense if you put spoil in its place, so ruin means spoil here. Ruin can also mean losing all your money: the business faced ruin.
fact: Ruin means to damage or spoil something so badly that it is no good any more.
fact: A ruin is what is left of an old building that has fallen down, such as a castle or a Roman fort.
fact: «Ruin» can also mean losing all your money: the business faced ruin.
fact: Useful phrases: in ruins, ruin the surprise, ruin someone's day, go to ruin.
fact: «The Rat is very cross: his boat is lost and his nice suit ruined.» Here ruined means spoilt.
exercise: «Rain ruined the picnic.» What does ruined mean? | Finished early and tidied up | Cooked in the sun | *Spoilt, so it was no good any more | Made bigger
exercise: In history we visited the ruins of an old abbey. What are the ruins? | *What is left of an old building that has fallen down | A brand new shop | A big picnic table | A kind of hat
exercise: «One speck of dust can ruin a chip.» Find and copy the word that means spoil. | *ruin | clean | speck | chip
test: «Muddy shoes ruin the carpet.» Which word could replace ruin without changing the meaning? | Admire | Dry | *Damage | Clean
test: «The business faced ruin.» What does ruin mean here? | *Losing all its money | Growing very big | Being in the newspaper | Having a party
exam: Ella says, «The castle is in ruins.» What does in ruins mean? | It has been moved to another hill | It is full of visitors and shops | *It has fallen down and is broken | It is brand new and freshly painted
